  "_comment": "Reference catalog for the SSL Inspection bypass workflow. Big platforms answer on dozens of hostnames, but only a handful actually break under TLS interception (certificate pinning, mutual TLS, device attestation) or carry data a company deliberately refuses to decrypt (sign-in, secrets, banking). Each entry says which is which so an admin bypasses 4-5 domains instead of the whole platform. 'recommended' marks the ones normally bypassed.",
